      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Season the chicken thighs with cumin, smoked paprika and turmeric. Heat the oil in a dutch oven over medium-high heat. Brown the chicken skin-side down for 6 minutes until deep golden. Turn and cook for 3 more minutes. Remove and set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Reduce the heat to medium. Add the onion to the same pot and cook for 5 minutes. Add the garlic, red and green pepper and cook for a further 4 minutes until soft."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the fresh tomatoes and tinned tomatoes. Cook for 5 minutes, breaking up the tinned tomatoes with a spoon, until the mixture reduces slightly. Add the bay leaves."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the rinsed rice and stir to coat in the tomato mixture. Pour in the hot chicken stock and stir well. Nestle the browned chicken pieces skin-side up on top of the rice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bring to a boil, then reduce to a very low simmer. Cover tightly and cook for 20 minutes. Turn off the heat and leave covered for 10 minutes. Remove the bay leaves, scatter with fresh coriander and serve from the pot."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Rice is undercooked and still hard"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add 100 ml more hot stock, replace the lid and cook for another 5 to 8 minutes. The rice may need more liquid depending on the variety used."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Rice is mushy and overcooked"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove the lid for the last 5 minutes of cooking to let excess moisture escape. Check at 18 minutes rather than 20 next time and use the resting period to finish cooking in residual heat."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Chicken skin is soft rather than crispy"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The skin softens once it sits in the steam of the covered pot. If a crispy skin is important, finish the dish under a hot grill for 4 minutes before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Arroz con Pollo is eaten from Puerto Rico to Colombia to Cuba to Spain. It crossed the Atlantic with Spanish settlers and was transformed by local ingredients everywhere it landed. In Cuba the rice is golden with saffron. In Colombia it is coloured with turmeric. In Puerto Rico sofrito is the base. Every version is good. Every family insists theirs is the original."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
